<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>GUID_TGT - star tracker blinding vs. elevation margin</title>
<style>
  :root{--bg:#10151c;--panel:#18202b;--line:#2a3646;--ink:#e6edf3;--mut:#8b98a8;
        --ok:#3ddc84;--earth:#ff5c5c;--sun:#ffb020;--acc:#4cc2ff;--eta:#ffd166;--eps:#7be0ad;--rho:#cfd8e3;}
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:14px/1.45 Segoe UI,system-ui,sans-serif}
  header{padding:14px 22px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  h1{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:20px}
  header p{margin:2px 0;color:var(--mut);max-width:1250px}
  .wrap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:330px 1fr;gap:14px;padding:14px 22px}
  .panel{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:12px}
  .panel h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:15px;color:var(--acc)}
  .ctl{margin:7px 0}
  .ctl label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px}
  .ctl label b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
  .ctl small{color:var(--mut);display:block;font-size:11.5px}
  input[type=range]{width:100%}
  button{background:#233044;color:var(--ink);border:1px solid #38485f;border-radius:6px;padding:5px 10px;
         margin:3px 4px 3px 0;cursor:pointer;font-size:12.5px}
  button:hover{background:#2c3e57}
  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px}
  canvas{display:block;background:#0b1016;border-radius:6px;margin:0 auto;cursor:grab;touch-action:none}
  canvas:active{cursor:grabbing}
  .tb{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:2px;margin:-2px 0 6px}
  .tb span{color:var(--mut);font-size:11.5px;margin-left:8px}
  .cap{color:var(--mut);font-size:12.5px;margin-top:6px}
  .badge{display:inline-block;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px}
  .b-ok{background:#12351f;color:var(--ok)} .b-bad{background:#4a1616;color:var(--earth)}
  .b-warn{background:#47340a;color:var(--sun)} .b-info{background:#12304a;color:var(--acc)}
  table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}
  td,th{padding:3px 6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left}
  .sw{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;margin-right:5px}
  .note{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--mut)}
  .note li{margin:2px 0}
  .gl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:6px}
  .gl div{background:#121923;border:1px solid var(--line);border-left-width:4px;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 10px;font-size:13px}
  .gl h3{margin:0 0 3px;font-size:14px}
  .gl p{margin:2px 0;color:#c4cfdb}
  @media(max-width:1100px){.wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <h1>GUID_TGT &mdash; why aiming at a target can blind the star trackers</h1>
  <p><b>Idea.</b> While aiming, the satellite points its +Z axis (payload) at the target, tilted by &eta; from nadir. The 3 star trackers look around &minus;Z (40&deg; cone), so the tilt swings one side of that cone toward the Earth horizon. A tracker whose boresight is within (&rho; + 22&deg;) &asymp; 90&deg; of nadir is blinded by the Earth; one within 35&deg; of the Sun is blinded by the Sun.</p>
  <p><b>The knob.</b> <code>tgtGuidElevationMargin</code>: aiming only starts when <code>&epsilon; + margin &gt; 0</code>. A negative margin = &minus;&epsilon;<sub>min</sub> caps the tilt: sin&eta; = (Re/r)&middot;cos&epsilon;.</p>
  <div class="gl">
    <div style="border-left-color:var(--eps)"><h3 style="color:var(--eps)">&epsilon; &mdash; elevation (measured at the TARGET)</h3>
      <p>Angle, <b>seen from the target T</b>, between the local horizon and the direction to the satellite. 0&deg; = satellite on the target's horizon, 90&deg; = satellite straight overhead.</p>
      <p>In the model (<i>Compute Satellite Elevation</i>): &epsilon; = 90&deg; &minus; acos( unit(sat &minus; target) &middot; unit(local normal at target) ). Now: <b id="g_eps"></b></p></div>
    <div style="border-left-color:var(--eta)"><h3 style="color:var(--eta)">&eta; &mdash; off-nadir (slew) angle (measured at the SATELLITE)</h3>
      <p>Angle <b>at the satellite S</b> between nadir (straight down to the Earth centre) and the line of sight to the target. It is how far +Z must be tilted away from nadir to point at the target.</p>
      <p>Linked to &epsilon; by the triangle Earth-centre / satellite / target: sin&eta; = (Re/r)&middot;cos&epsilon;. Low &epsilon; &rArr; large &eta;. Now: <b id="g_eta"></b></p></div>
    <div style="border-left-color:var(--rho)"><h3 style="color:var(--rho)">&rho; &mdash; Earth angular radius (measured at the SATELLITE)</h3>
      <p>Half-angle of the cone under which the satellite sees the Earth disk: angle <b>at S</b> between nadir and the Earth's limb (tangent ray). sin&rho; = Re/(Re+h).</p>
      <p>Largest possible &eta; (target on the horizon, &epsilon; = 0) equals &rho;. Now: <b id="g_rho"></b></p></div>
    <div style="border-left-color:var(--earth)"><h3 style="color:var(--earth)">&rho; + 22&deg; &mdash; star-tracker Earth blinding limit</h3>
      <p>A tracker is blinded if its boresight is within 22&deg; of the limb, i.e. within &rho; + 22&deg; of nadir. At 500 km this is &asymp; 90&deg;: <b>"below the local horizontal plane" = blinded</b>. Now: <b id="g_lim"></b></p>
      <p>Other symbols: r = Re + h (orbit radius), h = altitude, &lambda; = Earth-centre angle between sub-satellite point and target.</p></div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">
  <!-- ================= CONTROLS ================= -->
  <div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Orbit &amp; GUID_TGT</h2>
      <div class="ctl"><label>Altitude <b id="o_alt"></b></label><input id="alt" type="range" min="300" max="1000" step="10" value="500"></div>
      <div class="ctl"><label>tgtGuidElevationMargin <b id="o_margin"></b></label>
        <input id="margin" type="range" min="-60" max="30" step="0.5" value="0">
        <small>0 = model default. Negative = require a minimum elevation.</small></div>
      <div class="ctl"><label>Current target elevation &epsilon; <b id="o_eps"></b></label>
        <input id="eps" type="range" min="0" max="90" step="any" value="3">
        <small>Satellite elevation as seen from the target (0&deg; = target on the horizon).</small><small id="epsHint" style="color:#ffb020"></small></div>
      <div class="ctl"><label>Tilt azimuth &phi; <b id="o_phi"></b></label>
        <input id="phi" type="range" min="0" max="355" step="5" value="130">
        <small>Body azimuth (about &minus;Z) of the side that dips toward the Earth. Set by the yaw mode / target geometry.</small></div>
      <button id="btnSweep">&#9654; Sweep &phi;</button>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:14px">
      <h2>Sun</h2>
      <div class="ctl">
        <label><span><input type="radio" name="smode" value="manual" checked> Manual (any direction)</span>
        <span><input type="radio" name="smode" value="orbit"> Orbit-realistic</span></label>
      </div>
      <div id="sunManual">
        <div class="ctl"><label>Sun zenith angle <b id="o_ths"></b></label><input id="ths" type="range" min="0" max="180" step="1" value="45"></div>
        <div class="ctl"><label>Sun azimuth rel. to target dir. <b id="o_als"></b></label><input id="als" type="range" min="0" max="359" step="1" value="180"></div>
      </div>
      <div id="sunOrbit" style="display:none">
        <div class="ctl"><label>Beta angle &beta; <b id="o_beta"></b></label><input id="beta" type="range" min="0" max="90" step="1" value="22">
          <small>LTDN 10.5 h at 500 km: |&beta;| &asymp; 17&ndash;24&deg;</small></div>
        <div class="ctl"><label>Orbit phase &nu; (0 = sub-solar side) <b id="o_nu"></b></label><input id="nu" type="range" min="0" max="359" step="1" value="30"></div>
        <div class="ctl"><label>Target bearing from along-track <b id="o_brg"></b></label><input id="brg" type="range" min="0" max="359" step="1" value="90">
          <small>90&deg; = target purely cross-track.</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:14px">
      <h2>Shortcuts</h2>
      <button id="btnDefault">Margin = 0 (default)</button>
      <button id="btn2">Margin: &le;1 ST Earth-blinded</button>
      <button id="btnNB">Margin: no Earth blinding</button>
      <button id="btnFind">Find a full-blind case</button>
      <button id="btnRecenterAll">&#8634; Recenter all plots</button>
      <div id="findMsg" class="note" style="margin-top:6px"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= VISUALS ================= -->
  <div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>1 &middot; Orbit plane: the triangle Earth-centre / satellite / target (zoomed)</h2>
        <div class="tb" data-v="side"><button data-a="in">&#43; Zoom</button><button data-a="out">&minus; Zoom</button><button data-a="reset">&#8634; Recenter</button><span>drag = pan &middot; wheel = zoom &middot; double-click = recenter</span></div>
        <canvas id="cSide" width="520" height="470"></canvas>
        <div class="cap"><b style="color:var(--eta)">&eta;</b> at the satellite (nadir &rarr; target). <b style="color:var(--eps)">&epsilon;</b> at the target (horizon &rarr; satellite). <b style="color:var(--rho)">&rho;</b> at the satellite (nadir &rarr; limb). Red wedge = Earth-blinded directions (half-angle &rho;+22&deg; &asymp; 90&deg;). Dashed cone = trackers' 40&deg; view cone around &minus;Z; its edge turns red when it enters the wedge. The inset shows the same triangle un-zoomed (O = Earth centre).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>2 &middot; Star-tracker sky view (body frame, centred on &minus;Z)</h2>
        <div class="tb" data-v="sky"><button data-a="in">&#43; Zoom</button><button data-a="out">&minus; Zoom</button><button data-a="reset">&#8634; Recenter</button><span>drag = pan &middot; wheel = zoom &middot; double-click = recenter</span></div>
        <canvas id="cSky" width="520" height="470"></canvas>
        <div class="cap">Azimuthal projection, centre = &minus;Z_SBF (out to 130&deg;). Red = Earth exclusion region (cone of half-angle &rho;+22&deg; around nadir), yellow = Sun exclusion cone (35&deg;). A tracker dot inside red or yellow is blind. Aiming tilts the red region in from the &phi; side.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:14px">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>3 &middot; Elevation margin needed vs. altitude</h2>
        <div class="tb" data-v="curve"><button data-a="in">&#43; Zoom</button><button data-a="out">&minus; Zoom</button><button data-a="reset">&#8634; Recenter</button><span>drag = pan &middot; wheel = zoom &middot; double-click = recenter</span></div>
        <canvas id="cCurve" width="520" height="330"></canvas>
        <div class="cap">Above the green curve no tracker can ever be Earth-blinded (Sun alone can never blind all 3). Above the amber curve at most one can be. Red = margin 0 (aim down to the horizon).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Readout</h2>
        <div id="state"></div>
        <table id="stTable" style="margin-top:8px"></table>
        <div id="tri" style="margin-top:10px"></div>
        <div id="worst" style="margin-top:10px"></div>
        <div id="thr" style="margin-top:10px"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:14px">
      <h2>Assumptions (to verify numerically against the model)</h2>
      <ul class="note">
        <li>Tracker geometry from <code>hwDB.m</code>: boresights 40&deg; from &minus;Z_SBF (polar angle 140&deg; from +Z), azimuths 80/180/280&deg;. The two possible rotation conventions give mirrored layouts and identical results.</li>
        <li>Target-pointing axis assumed to be +Z_SBF (depends on <code>tgtGuidOffset = [0.5 0.5 0.5 0.5]</code>).</li>
        <li>Earth exclusion (22&deg;) measured from the Earth limb; Sun exclusion 35&deg; from the boresight; spherical Earth, circular orbit; no pointing error and no slew dynamics.</li>
        <li>Orbit-realistic Sun: local components (cos&beta;cos&nu;, &minus;cos&beta;sin&nu;, sin&beta;) in (zenith, along-track, cross-track); no Sun blinding in eclipse.</li>
        <li>Worst-case scan covers all tilt azimuths &phi; and, in manual mode, all Sun directions (or, in orbit mode, all &nu; and target bearings at the chosen &beta;), at the largest tilt the margin allows. &phi; is treated as independent of the Sun (conservative).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
'use strict';
// ------------------------------------------------------------------ constants
const RE = 6378.137, EEA = 22, SEA = 35, STTH = 40, STAZ = [80, 180, 280];
const D2R = Math.PI / 180, R2D = 180 / Math.PI;
const COL = {ok:'#3ddc84', earth:'#ff5c5c', sun:'#ffb020', acc:'#4cc2ff', mut:'#8b98a8', eta:'#ffd166', eps:'#7be0ad', rho:'#cfd8e3'};

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ vector helpers
const V = {
  add:(a,b)=>[a[0]+b[0],a[1]+b[1],a[2]+b[2]],
  sc:(a,s)=>[a[0]*s,a[1]*s,a[2]*s],
  dot:(a,b)=>a[0]*b[0]+a[1]*b[1]+a[2]*b[2],
  cross:(a,b)=>[a[1]*b[2]-a[2]*b[1],a[2]*b[0]-a[0]*b[2],a[0]*b[1]-a[1]*b[0]],
  neg:a=>[-a[0],-a[1],-a[2]],
  norm:a=>{const n=Math.hypot(a[0],a[1],a[2]);return [a[0]/n,a[1]/n,a[2]/n];}
};
const angDeg = (a,b)=>Math.acos(Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,V.dot(a,b))))*R2D;

// ST boresights in SBF (unit vectors). Polar angle STTH from -Z, azimuth STAZ.
const BORE = STAZ.map(a=>[Math.sin(STTH*D2R)*Math.cos(a*D2R), Math.sin(STTH*D2R)*Math.sin(a*D2R), -Math.cos(STTH*D2R)]);

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ geometry
const rhoOf  = r => Math.asin(RE/r)*R2D;                       // Earth angular radius [deg]
const etaOf  = (eps,r) => Math.asin(Math.min(1, RE/r*Math.cos(eps*D2R)))*R2D;   // off-nadir slew for elevation eps
const epsOf  = (eta,r) => { const c = Math.sin(eta*D2R)*r/RE; return c>=1 ? 0 : Math.acos(c)*R2D; };

// Local frame expressed in SBF. phi = body azimuth (about -Z) of the side dipping toward the Earth.
// Pointing axis +Z is tilted eta from nadir toward the target.
function frame(etaDeg, phiDeg){
  const e = etaDeg*D2R, wa = (phiDeg+180)*D2R;
  const w = [Math.cos(wa), Math.sin(wa), 0];
  const z = V.add(V.sc([0,0,-1],Math.cos(e)), V.sc(w,Math.sin(e)));   // zenith
  const h = V.add(V.sc([0,0, 1],Math.sin(e)), V.sc(w,Math.cos(e)));   // horizontal dir. toward target
  const k = V.cross(z,h);
  return {z,h,k,n:V.neg(z)};
}

// Sun direction in local components (sz = zenith, sh = toward target, sk = z x h)
function sunLocal(mode, p, r){
  if(mode==='manual'){
    const t=p.ths*D2R, a=p.als*D2R;
    return {sz:Math.cos(t), sh:Math.sin(t)*Math.cos(a), sk:Math.sin(t)*Math.sin(a), ecl:false};
  }
  const b=p.beta*D2R, nu=p.nu*D2R, br=p.brg*D2R;
  const sz=Math.cos(b)*Math.cos(nu), sa=-Math.cos(b)*Math.sin(nu), sc=Math.sin(b);
  const ecl = sz<0 && Math.sqrt(1-sz*sz) < RE/r;
  return {sz, sh:sa*Math.cos(br)+sc*Math.sin(br), sk:-sa*Math.sin(br)+sc*Math.cos(br), ecl};
}
const sunBody = (s,f)=> V.add(V.add(V.sc(f.z,s.sz), V.sc(f.h,s.sh)), V.sc(f.k,s.sk));

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ thresholds & worst-case scan
function thresholds(alt){
  const r=RE+alt, rho=rhoOf(r), lim=rho+EEA;
  const etaNB = Math.max(0, 180-lim-STTH);
  let eta2 = 90;
  outer: for(let e=0;e<=90;e+=0.1){
    for(let p=0;p<360;p+=2){
      const f=frame(e,p); let c=0;
      for(const b of BORE) if(angDeg(b,f.n)<lim) c++;
      if(c>=2){ eta2=e; break outer; }
    }
  }
  return {r,rho,lim,etaNB,eta2,epsNB:epsOf(etaNB,r),eps2:epsOf(eta2,r)};
}

const sunSetCache = {};
function sunSet(mode, beta, r){
  const key = mode+'|'+beta+'|'+r;
  if(sunSetCache[key]) return sunSetCache[key];
  const arr=[];
  if(mode==='manual'){
    for(let t=0;t<=180;t+=6) for(let a=0;a<360;a+=12)
      arr.push({s:sunLocal('manual',{ths:t,als:a},r), cfg:{ths:t,als:a}});
  } else {
    for(let nu=0;nu<360;nu+=5) for(let b=0;b<360;b+=10)
      arr.push({s:sunLocal('orbit',{beta,nu,brg:b},r), cfg:{nu,brg:b}});
  }
  return sunSetCache[key]=arr;
}

function scan(etaWc, r, mode, beta){
  const lim = rhoOf(r)+EEA, cs = Math.cos(SEA*D2R), sunS = sunSet(mode,beta,r);
  let maxEarth=0, minAvail=3, arg=null;
  for(let phi=0;phi<360;phi+=5){
    const f=frame(etaWc,phi);
    const eb = BORE.map(b=>angDeg(b,f.n)<lim);
    const nE = eb.filter(Boolean).length; if(nE>maxEarth) maxEarth=nE;
    for(const q of sunS){
      let avail=0;
      if(q.s.ecl){ avail = 3-nE; }
      else {
        const sb=sunBody(q.s,f);
        for(let i=0;i<3;i++) if(!eb[i] && V.dot(BORE[i],sb)<=cs) avail++;
      }
      if(avail<minAvail){ minAvail=avail; arg={phi,cfg:q.cfg}; }
    }
  }
  return {maxEarth,minAvail,arg};
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ canvases, views (zoom / pan)
function setup(c){
  const d=window.devicePixelRatio||1, w=c.width, h=c.height;
  c.width=w*d; c.height=h*d; c.style.width=w+'px'; c.style.height=h+'px';
  const x=c.getContext('2d'); x.setTransform(d,0,0,d,0,0); x.W=w; x.H=h; return x;
}
const cs_ = setup(document.getElementById('cSide'));
const ck_ = setup(document.getElementById('cSky'));
const cc_ = setup(document.getElementById('cCurve'));

// view: z = zoom, (tx,ty) = pan in px, (cx,cy) = zoom reference point (screen px)
const SIDE_PAD = {l:190, r:110, t:70, b:95};
const VIEW = {
  side :{z:1,tx:0,ty:0,cx:(cs_.W+SIDE_PAD.l-SIDE_PAD.r)/2, cy:(cs_.H+SIDE_PAD.t-SIDE_PAD.b)/2, el:cs_},
  sky  :{z:1,tx:0,ty:0,cx:ck_.W/2, cy:ck_.H/2, el:ck_},
  curve:{z:1,tx:0,ty:0,cx:48+(cc_.W-48-14)/2, cy:14+(cc_.H-14-40)/2, el:cc_}
};
const ZMIN=0.4, ZMAX=14;
function zoomAt(v,f,mx,my){
  const nz=Math.max(ZMIN,Math.min(ZMAX,v.z*f)), k=nz/v.z;
  v.tx=(mx-v.cx)-(mx-v.cx-v.tx)*k; v.ty=(my-v.cy)-(my-v.cy-v.ty)*k; v.z=nz;
}
const resetView=v=>{ v.z=1; v.tx=0; v.ty=0; };

function arcBetween(g,cx,cy,rad,a1,a2){      // short arc between two canvas angles; returns mid angle
  let da=a2-a1; while(da>Math.PI)da-=2*Math.PI; while(da<-Math.PI)da+=2*Math.PI;
  g.beginPath(); g.arc(cx,cy,rad,a1,a1+da,da<0); g.stroke();
  return a1+da/2;
}
function label(g,t,x,y,col,al,font){ g.fillStyle=col||'#e6edf3'; g.textAlign=al||'left'; g.font=font||'12px Segoe UI'; g.fillText(t,x,y); }
function tag(g,t,x,y,col,al,font){   // text on a dark backing box (legible over any background)
  g.font=font||'12px Segoe UI'; const w=g.measureText(t).width; let bx=x;
  if(al==='center') bx=x-w/2; else if(al==='right') bx=x-w;
  g.fillStyle='rgba(11,16,22,.80)'; g.fillRect(bx-3,y-12,w+6,16);
  g.textAlign=al||'left'; g.fillStyle=col||'#e6edf3'; g.fillText(t,x,y);
}
function arrow(g,x0,y0,x1,y1,col,w){
  g.strokeStyle=col; g.fillStyle=col; g.lineWidth=w||2;
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(x0,y0); g.lineTo(x1,y1); g.stroke();
  const a=Math.atan2(y1-y0,x1-x0), s=9;
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(x1,y1); g.lineTo(x1-s*Math.cos(a-0.4),y1-s*Math.sin(a-0.4)); g.lineTo(x1-s*Math.cos(a+0.4),y1-s*Math.sin(a+0.4)); g.closePath(); g.fill();
  g.lineWidth=1;
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ 1 - side view (world units: km, origin = Earth centre, y up)
function drawSide(S){
  const g=cs_, W=g.W, H=g.H, v=VIEW.side;
  g.clearRect(0,0,W,H);
  const r=S.r, epsT=S.eps, etaT=etaOf(epsT,r), lam=(90-epsT-etaT)*D2R;
  const Sw=[0,r], Tw=[RE*Math.sin(lam),RE*Math.cos(lam)];
  // auto-fit on satellite, target and sub-satellite point
  const minx=Math.min(0,Tw[0]), maxx=Math.max(0,Tw[0]), maxy=r, miny=Tw[1];
  const bw=Math.max(maxx-minx,1e-6), bh=Math.max(maxy-miny,1e-6);
  const s0=Math.min((W-SIDE_PAD.l-SIDE_PAD.r)/bw,(H-SIDE_PAD.t-SIDE_PAD.b)/bh);
  const bxc=(minx+maxx)/2, byc=(miny+maxy)/2, sc=s0*v.z;
  const P=(x,y)=>[v.cx+v.tx+sc*(x-bxc), v.cy+v.ty-sc*(y-byc)];
  const dirS=a=>[Math.sin(a*D2R),Math.cos(a*D2R)];            // screen dir for "angle from nadir toward +x"
  const O=P(0,0), Sp=P(Sw[0],Sw[1]), Tp=P(Tw[0],Tw[1]), Np=P(0,RE), Rpx=RE*sc;
  const lim=S.rho+EEA;

  g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(0,0,W,H); g.clip();

  // Earth-exclusion wedge
  g.fillStyle='rgba(255,92,92,.15)'; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]);
  for(let a=-lim;a<=lim;a+=2){ const d=dirS(a); g.lineTo(Sp[0]+3000*d[0],Sp[1]+3000*d[1]); }
  g.closePath(); g.fill();
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,92,92,.85)'; g.setLineDash([6,4]);
  for(const s of [-1,1]){ const d=dirS(s*lim); g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]); g.lineTo(Sp[0]+3000*d[0],Sp[1]+3000*d[1]); g.stroke(); }
  g.setLineDash([]);

  // Earth
  g.fillStyle='#16466f'; g.beginPath(); g.arc(O[0],O[1],Rpx,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
  g.strokeStyle='#2f7fc0'; g.lineWidth=2; g.stroke(); g.lineWidth=1;

  // triangle O - S - T (O is usually off-screen below)
  g.fillStyle='rgba(255,209,102,.08)'; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]); g.lineTo(Tp[0],Tp[1]); g.lineTo(O[0],O[1]); g.closePath(); g.fill();
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.45)'; g.setLineDash([2,4]);
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]); g.lineTo(O[0],O[1]); g.stroke();            // O-S radial (through nadir)
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Tp[0],Tp[1]); g.lineTo(O[0],O[1]); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);  // O-T radial
  tag(g,'towards Earth centre O (r = '+r.toFixed(0)+' km)',Np[0]+8,Np[1]+Math.min(40,Math.max(14,(H-Np[1])/2)),COL.rho,'left','11px Segoe UI');

  // limb rays (angle rho)
  const Lt=Math.sqrt(r*r-RE*RE)*sc;
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.55)';
  for(const s of [-1,1]){ const d=dirS(s*S.rho); g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]); g.lineTo(Sp[0]+Lt*d[0],Sp[1]+Lt*d[1]); g.stroke(); }

  // local horizon at S and nadir marker
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.28)'; g.setLineDash([2,4]);
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0]-230,Sp[1]); g.lineTo(Sp[0]+230,Sp[1]); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);
  tag(g,'local horizon at S',Sp[0]-228,Sp[1]-6,COL.mut,'left','11px Segoe UI');
  g.fillStyle='#fff'; g.beginPath(); g.arc(Np[0],Np[1],4,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
  tag(g,'nadir point',Np[0]-8,Np[1]+16,'#fff','right','11px Segoe UI');
  tag(g,'h = '+S.alt+' km',Sp[0]-6,(Sp[1]+Np[1])/2,COL.mut,'right','11px Segoe UI');

  // local vertical + horizon at target
  const radT=[Math.sin(lam),-Math.cos(lam)];            // outward radial, screen
  const tanT=[-Math.cos(lam),-Math.sin(lam)];           // tangent toward satellite side, screen
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(123,224,173,.75)'; g.setLineDash([4,4]);
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Tp[0],Tp[1]); g.lineTo(Tp[0]+120*radT[0],Tp[1]+120*radT[1]); g.stroke();
  g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Tp[0]-110*tanT[0],Tp[1]-110*tanT[1]); g.lineTo(Tp[0]+150*tanT[0],Tp[1]+150*tanT[1]); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);
  tag(g,'local vertical at T',Tp[0]+124*radT[0]+4,Tp[1]+124*radT[1],COL.eps,'left','11px Segoe UI');
  tag(g,'local horizon at T',Tp[0]-108*tanT[0],Tp[1]-108*tanT[1]-6,COL.eps,'left','11px Segoe UI');

  // line of sight
  g.strokeStyle='#ff7ad9'; g.lineWidth=1.8; g.setLineDash([7,4]); g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]); g.lineTo(Tp[0],Tp[1]); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]); g.lineWidth=1;
  const d_km=Math.sqrt(r*r+RE*RE-2*r*RE*Math.cos(lam));
  tag(g,'line of sight  d = '+d_km.toFixed(0)+' km',(Sp[0]+Tp[0])/2+8,(Sp[1]+Tp[1])/2-6,'#ff7ad9','left','11px Segoe UI');
  g.fillStyle='#ff7ad9'; g.beginPath(); g.arc(Tp[0],Tp[1],5,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
  tag(g,'target T',Tp[0]+8,Tp[1]+18,'#ff7ad9');

  // satellite axes
  const eta=S.eta, pz=dirS(eta), mz=[-pz[0],-pz[1]];
  arrow(g,Sp[0],Sp[1],Sp[0]+95*pz[0],Sp[1]+95*pz[1],'#ffffff',2.5);
  arrow(g,Sp[0],Sp[1],Sp[0]+80*mz[0],Sp[1]+80*mz[1],COL.acc,2.5);
  tag(g,'+Z (payload)',Sp[0]+98*pz[0]+4,Sp[1]+98*pz[1]+14,'#fff');
  tag(g,'−Z',Sp[0]+84*mz[0]-4,Sp[1]+84*mz[1]-4,COL.acc,'right');
  // ST view cone edges
  for(const s of [-1,1]){
    const a=((180+eta+s*STTH)%360+360)%360, fromNadir=a>180?360-a:a, d=dirS(a);
    g.strokeStyle = fromNadir<lim ? COL.earth : COL.ok; g.lineWidth=2; g.setLineDash([7,4]);
    g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Sp[0],Sp[1]); g.lineTo(Sp[0]+135*d[0],Sp[1]+135*d[1]); g.stroke();
    g.setLineDash([]); g.lineWidth=1;
    tag(g,'ST cone edge: '+fromNadir.toFixed(0)+'° from nadir',Sp[0]+140*d[0]+(d[0]<0?-4:4),Sp[1]+140*d[1]+(d[1]<0?-2:12),
        fromNadir<lim?COL.earth:COL.ok,d[0]<0?'right':'left','11px Segoe UI');
  }
  g.fillStyle='#dfe7f0'; g.fillRect(Sp[0]-5,Sp[1]-5,10,10);
  tag(g,'satellite S',Sp[0]+10,Sp[1]-10,'#dfe7f0');

  // ---- angle arcs
  g.lineWidth=1.6;
  g.strokeStyle=COL.rho;                       // rho: nadir -> limb (left)
  let m=arcBetween(g,Sp[0],Sp[1],86,Math.PI/2,Math.PI/2+S.rho*D2R);
  tag(g,'ρ = '+S.rho.toFixed(1)+'° (limb)',Sp[0]+96*Math.cos(m)-4,Sp[1]+96*Math.sin(m),COL.rho,'right','12px Segoe UI');
  g.strokeStyle=COL.earth;                     // rho+22: nadir -> exclusion edge (left)
  m=arcBetween(g,Sp[0],Sp[1],122,Math.PI/2,Math.PI/2+lim*D2R);
  tag(g,'ρ+22° = '+lim.toFixed(1)+'°',Sp[0]+130*Math.cos(m)-4,Sp[1]+130*Math.sin(m)+4,COL.earth,'right','12px Segoe UI');
  g.strokeStyle=COL.eta;                       // eta: nadir -> line of sight (right)
  if(etaT>0.3){ m=arcBetween(g,Sp[0],Sp[1],58,Math.PI/2,Math.PI/2-etaT*D2R);
    tag(g,'η = '+etaT.toFixed(1)+'°'+(S.aiming?'':' (not applied)'),Sp[0]+68*Math.cos(m)+2,Sp[1]+68*Math.sin(m)+4,COL.eta,'left','12px Segoe UI'); }
  g.strokeStyle=COL.eps;                       // epsilon at T: horizon -> satellite
  const aEt=Math.atan2(tanT[1],tanT[0]), aTS=Math.atan2(Sp[1]-Tp[1],Sp[0]-Tp[0]);
  m=arcBetween(g,Tp[0],Tp[1],46,aEt,aTS);
  tag(g,'ε = '+epsT.toFixed(1)+'°',Tp[0]+60*Math.cos(m),Tp[1]+60*Math.sin(m)+4,COL.eps,'center','12px Segoe UI');
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(200,170,255,.9)';        // interior angle at T (T->O to T->S) = 90 + eps
  const aTO=Math.atan2(Math.cos(lam),-Math.sin(lam));
  m=arcBetween(g,Tp[0],Tp[1],30,aTO,aTS);
  tag(g,'90°+ε = '+(90+epsT).toFixed(1)+'°',Tp[0]+44*Math.cos(m)-4,Tp[1]+44*Math.sin(m)+14,'#c8aaff','right','11px Segoe UI');
  g.lineWidth=1;

  g.restore();

  // inset: whole triangle un-zoomed
  const ix=W-166, iy=8, iw=158, ih=158, Ri=40, ri=Ri*r/RE;
  const Oc=[ix+iw/2, iy+ih/2+ri*0.5+4], S2=[Oc[0],Oc[1]-ri], T2=[Oc[0]+Ri*Math.sin(lam),Oc[1]-Ri*Math.cos(lam)];
  g.fillStyle='rgba(11,16,22,.92)'; g.fillRect(ix,iy,iw,ih); g.strokeStyle='#2a3646'; g.strokeRect(ix,iy,iw,ih);
  g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(ix,iy,iw,ih); g.clip();
  g.fillStyle='#16466f'; g.beginPath(); g.arc(Oc[0],Oc[1],Ri,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.3)'; g.setLineDash([3,3]); g.beginPath(); g.arc(Oc[0],Oc[1],ri,0,2*Math.PI); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);
  g.fillStyle='rgba(255,209,102,.18)'; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Oc[0],Oc[1]); g.lineTo(S2[0],S2[1]); g.lineTo(T2[0],T2[1]); g.closePath(); g.fill();
  g.strokeStyle='#ffd166'; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(Oc[0],Oc[1]); g.lineTo(S2[0],S2[1]); g.lineTo(T2[0],T2[1]); g.closePath(); g.stroke();
  g.fillStyle='#dfe7f0'; g.fillRect(S2[0]-3,S2[1]-3,6,6);
  g.fillStyle='#ff7ad9'; g.beginPath(); g.arc(T2[0],T2[1],3,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
  label(g,'S',S2[0]+6,S2[1]+4,'#dfe7f0','left','11px Segoe UI'); label(g,'T',T2[0]+6,T2[1]-2,'#ff7ad9','left','11px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'O',Oc[0]-12,Oc[1]+4,'#fff','left','11px Segoe UI');
  g.restore();
  label(g,'λ = '+(lam*R2D).toFixed(1)+'° at O',ix+6,iy+ih-6,'#cfd8e3','left','10.5px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'full triangle (not zoomed)',ix+6,iy+12,COL.mut,'left','10.5px Segoe UI');

  tag(g,S.aiming?'AIMING: +Z follows the target':'WAITING: +Z held at nadir (η applied = 0)',10,20,S.aiming?COL.sun:COL.ok,'left','13px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'zoom ×'+v.z.toFixed(2),10,H-8,COL.mut,'left','11px Segoe UI');
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ 2 - sky view
function projSky(v,k,cx,cy){
  const th=Math.acos(Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,-v[2])))*R2D, ph=Math.atan2(v[1],v[0]);
  return [cx+k*th*Math.cos(ph), cy-k*th*Math.sin(ph), th];
}
function capPath(g,c,angDegCap,k,cx,cy){
  let u=Math.abs(c[2])<0.9?[0,0,1]:[1,0,0]; u=V.norm(V.cross(c,u)); const v=V.cross(c,u);
  const a=angDegCap*D2R; g.beginPath();
  for(let t=0;t<=360;t+=2){
    const tt=t*D2R;
    const p=V.add(V.sc(c,Math.cos(a)),V.add(V.sc(u,Math.sin(a)*Math.cos(tt)),V.sc(v,Math.sin(a)*Math.sin(tt))));
    const q=projSky(p,k,cx,cy); t===0?g.moveTo(q[0],q[1]):g.lineTo(q[0],q[1]);
  }
  g.closePath();
  return angDeg(c,[0,0,1])<angDegCap;    // true if cap contains +Z (outer singular point of the projection)
}
function capLabel(g,c,ang,text,col,k,cx,cy){   // label on the cap boundary, on the side facing -Z
  const mz=[0,0,-1], d=V.norm(V.add(mz,V.sc(c,-V.dot(mz,c))));
  const p=V.add(V.sc(c,Math.cos(ang*D2R)),V.sc(d,Math.sin(ang*D2R))), q=projSky(p,k,cx,cy);
  tag(g,text,q[0]+4,q[1]-4,col,'left','11px Segoe UI');
}
function drawSky(S){
  const g=ck_, v=VIEW.sky; g.clearRect(0,0,g.W,g.H);
  const cx=g.W/2, cy=g.H/2+4, Rv=205, k=Rv/130;
  g.save(); g.translate(v.cx+v.tx,v.cy+v.ty); g.scale(v.z,v.z); g.translate(-v.cx,-v.cy);
  g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.arc(cx,cy,Rv,0,2*Math.PI); g.clip();
  g.fillStyle='#0d1d33'; g.fillRect(0,0,g.W,g.H);

  // Earth region
  const cont=capPath(g,S.f.n,S.lim,k,cx,cy);
  g.fillStyle='rgba(255,92,92,.30)';
  if(cont){ g.moveTo(cx+k*180,cy); g.arc(cx,cy,k*180,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill('evenodd'); capPath(g,S.f.n,S.lim,k,cx,cy); }
  else g.fill();
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,92,92,.9)'; g.lineWidth=1.5; g.stroke(); g.lineWidth=1;
  capPath(g,S.f.n,S.rho,k,cx,cy); g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.4)'; g.setLineDash([3,4]); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);

  // Sun cone
  if(!S.sunEcl){
    const contS=capPath(g,S.sb,SEA,k,cx,cy);
    g.fillStyle='rgba(255,176,32,.22)';
    if(contS){ g.moveTo(cx+k*180,cy); g.arc(cx,cy,k*180,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill('evenodd'); capPath(g,S.sb,SEA,k,cx,cy); } else g.fill();
    g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,176,32,.9)'; g.stroke();
  }

  // grid
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.12)';
  for(const t of [30,60,90,120]){ g.beginPath(); g.arc(cx,cy,k*t,0,2*Math.PI); g.stroke(); }
  for(let a=0;a<360;a+=30){ g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(cx,cy); g.lineTo(cx+Rv*Math.cos(a*D2R),cy-Rv*Math.sin(a*D2R)); g.stroke(); }
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(76,194,255,.55)'; g.setLineDash([4,4]); g.beginPath(); g.arc(cx,cy,k*STTH,0,2*Math.PI); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);

  // zenith / nadir / Sun markers
  const zp=projSky(S.f.z,k,cx,cy);
  g.strokeStyle='#fff'; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(zp[0]-6,zp[1]); g.lineTo(zp[0]+6,zp[1]); g.moveTo(zp[0],zp[1]-6); g.lineTo(zp[0],zp[1]+6); g.stroke();
  label(g,'zenith',zp[0]+8,zp[1]-6,'#fff','left','11px Segoe UI');
  const np=projSky(S.f.n,k,cx,cy);
  if(np[2]<=130){ g.fillStyle=COL.earth; g.beginPath(); g.arc(np[0],np[1],4,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill(); label(g,'nadir',np[0]+7,np[1]+4,COL.earth,'left','11px Segoe UI'); }
  const sp=projSky(S.sb,k,cx,cy);
  if(sp[2]<=130){ g.fillStyle=S.sunEcl?'#777':COL.sun; g.beginPath(); g.arc(sp[0],sp[1],7,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
                  label(g,S.sunEcl?'Sun (eclipse)':'Sun',sp[0]+10,sp[1]-8,S.sunEcl?'#999':COL.sun,'left','12px Segoe UI'); }
  capLabel(g,S.f.n,S.lim,'Earth exclusion ρ+22°',COL.earth,k,cx,cy);
  capLabel(g,S.f.n,S.rho,'limb ρ',COL.rho,k,cx,cy);
  g.restore();

  for(const t of [30,60,90,120]) label(g,t+'°',cx+k*t*0.707+2,cy-k*t*0.707-2,COL.mut,'left','10px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'az 0° (+X)',cx+Rv+4,cy+4,COL.mut,'left','10px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'90° (+Y)',cx,cy-Rv-5,COL.mut,'center','10px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'180°',cx-Rv-4,cy+4,COL.mut,'right','10px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'270°',cx,cy+Rv+13,COL.mut,'center','10px Segoe UI');

  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    const p=projSky(BORE[i],k,cx,cy), st=S.st[i];
    const col = st.earth?COL.earth:(st.sun?COL.sun:COL.ok);
    g.fillStyle=col; g.strokeStyle=st.earth&&st.sun?COL.sun:'#0b1016'; g.lineWidth=st.earth&&st.sun?3:2;
    g.beginPath(); g.arc(p[0],p[1],11,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill(); g.stroke(); g.lineWidth=1;
    label(g,'ST'+(i+1),p[0],p[1]+4,'#0b1016','center','bold 11px Segoe UI');
  }
  g.restore();
  label(g,'centre = −Z_SBF · payload axis +Z is at the outer edge (180°)',g.W/2,g.H-4,COL.mut,'center','10px Segoe UI');
  label(g,'zoom ×'+v.z.toFixed(2),8,14,COL.mut,'left','11px Segoe UI');
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ 3 - margin curves
const CURVE=[]; (function(){ for(let a=300;a<=1000;a+=25){ const t=thresholds(a); CURVE.push({a,nb:t.epsNB,e2:t.eps2,hz:0}); } })();
function niceStep(range){ const raw=range/6, p=Math.pow(10,Math.floor(Math.log10(raw))), m=raw/p; return (m<1.5?1:m<3.5?2:m<7.5?5:10)*p; }
function drawCurve(S,T){
  const g=cc_, v=VIEW.curve; g.clearRect(0,0,g.W,g.H);
  const L=48,R=14,Tp=14,B=40, w=g.W-L-R, h=g.H-Tp-B, Lc=L+w/2, Tc=Tp+h/2;
  const X=a=>Lc+v.tx+v.z*(a-650)/700*w, Y=e=>Tc+v.ty-v.z*(e-30)/60*h;
  const aLo=650+(L-Lc-v.tx)/(v.z*w)*700, aHi=650+(L+w-Lc-v.tx)/(v.z*w)*700;
  const eHi=30-(Tp-Tc-v.ty)/(v.z*h)*60, eLo=30-(Tp+h-Tc-v.ty)/(v.z*h)*60;
  g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(L,Tp,w,h); g.clip();
  g.strokeStyle='#2a3646';
  const ea=niceStep(aHi-aLo), ee=niceStep(eHi-eLo);
  for(let a=Math.ceil(aLo/ea)*ea;a<=aHi;a+=ea){ g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(X(a),Tp); g.lineTo(X(a),Tp+h); g.stroke(); }
  for(let e=Math.ceil(eLo/ee)*ee;e<=eHi;e+=ee){ g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(L,Y(e)); g.lineTo(L+w,Y(e)); g.stroke(); }
  g.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.35)'; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(L,Y(0)); g.lineTo(L+w,Y(0)); g.stroke();
  const line=(key,col,dash)=>{ g.strokeStyle=col; g.lineWidth=2.2; g.setLineDash(dash||[]); g.beginPath();
    CURVE.forEach((p,i)=>{ i?g.lineTo(X(p.a),Y(p[key])):g.moveTo(X(p.a),Y(p[key])); }); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]); g.lineWidth=1; };
  line('nb',COL.ok); line('e2',COL.sun); line('hz',COL.earth,[5,4]);
  label(g,'no Earth blinding',X(640),Y(CURVE[14].nb)-8,COL.ok,'left');
  label(g,'≤1 ST Earth-blinded',X(640),Y(CURVE[14].e2)-8,COL.sun,'left');
  label(g,'margin = 0 (default)',X(640),Y(0)-6,COL.earth,'left');
  const eMin=Math.max(0,-S.margin);
  g.strokeStyle=COL.acc; g.setLineDash([6,4]); g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(L,Y(eMin)); g.lineTo(L+w,Y(eMin)); g.stroke(); g.setLineDash([]);
  label(g,'your ε_min = '+eMin.toFixed(1)+'°',L+6,Y(eMin)-5,COL.acc);
  g.strokeStyle=COL.acc; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(X(S.alt),Tp); g.lineTo(X(S.alt),Tp+h); g.stroke();
  g.fillStyle=COL.acc; g.beginPath(); g.arc(X(S.alt),Y(eMin),5,0,2*Math.PI); g.fill();
  g.restore();
  // axes labels (outside clip)
  g.fillStyle=COL.mut; g.font='11px Segoe UI'; g.textAlign='right';
  for(let e=Math.ceil(eLo/ee)*ee;e<=eHi;e+=ee) g.fillText(+e.toFixed(2)+'°',L-5,Y(e)+4);
  g.textAlign='center';
  for(let a=Math.ceil(aLo/ea)*ea;a<=aHi;a+=ea) g.fillText(+a.toFixed(2),X(a),Tp+h+14);
  g.fillText('altitude [km]',L+w/2,g.H-6);
  g.save(); g.translate(12,Tp+h/2); g.rotate(-Math.PI/2); g.fillText('minimum elevation ε_min = −margin',0,0); g.restore();
  g.strokeStyle='#2a3646'; g.strokeRect(L,Tp,w,h);
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ UI state & update
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
const IDS=['alt','margin','eps','phi','ths','als','beta','nu','brg'];
function readState(){
  const s={}; IDS.forEach(i=>s[i]=parseFloat($(i).value));
  s.smode=document.querySelector('input[name=smode]:checked').value;
  s.r=RE+s.alt; s.rho=rhoOf(s.r); s.lim=s.rho+EEA;
  s.aiming = s.eps + s.margin > 0;
  s.eta = s.aiming ? etaOf(s.eps,s.r) : 0;
  s.f = frame(s.eta,s.phi);
  const sl=sunLocal(s.smode,{ths:s.ths,als:s.als,beta:s.beta,nu:s.nu,brg:s.brg},s.r);
  s.sunEcl=sl.ecl; s.sb=sunBody(sl,s.f);
  s.thetaS=Math.acos(Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,sl.sz)))*R2D;
  const cs=Math.cos(SEA*D2R);
  s.st=BORE.map(b=>({earth:angDeg(b,s.f.n)<s.lim, sun:!s.sunEcl && V.dot(b,s.sb)>cs, angN:angDeg(b,s.f.n), angS:angDeg(b,s.sb)}));
  return s;
}
const badge=(t,c)=>'<span class="badge b-'+c+'">'+t+'</span>';
function redraw(){ if(!window._S) return; drawSide(window._S); drawSky(window._S); drawCurve(window._S,window._T); }

function update(){
  const S=readState(), T=thresholds(S.alt);
  $('o_alt').textContent=S.alt+' km';
  $('o_margin').textContent=S.margin.toFixed(1)+'° ('+(S.margin*D2R).toFixed(3)+' rad)';
  $('o_eps').textContent=S.eps.toFixed(1)+'°';
  $('o_phi').textContent=S.phi+'°';
  $('o_ths').textContent=S.ths+'°'; $('o_als').textContent=S.als+'°';
  $('o_beta').textContent=S.beta+'°'; $('o_nu').textContent=S.nu+'°'; $('o_brg').textContent=S.brg+'°';
  $('sunManual').style.display=S.smode==='manual'?'':'none';
  $('sunOrbit').style.display=S.smode==='orbit'?'':'none';

  const eE=Math.max(0,-S.margin), etaT=etaOf(S.eps,S.r), lam=90-S.eps-etaT;
  $('epsHint').innerHTML = S.margin<0 ? 'Aiming starts at ε = '+eE.toFixed(1)+'°: below it WAITING (η = 0), above it η = '+etaOf(eE+0.001,S.r).toFixed(1)+'° &mdash; a step, as in the model.' : 'Margin ≥ 0: always aiming (η follows ε continuously).';
  $('g_eps').textContent=S.eps.toFixed(1)+'°'; $('g_eta').textContent=etaT.toFixed(1)+'°'+(S.aiming?'':' (not applied: waiting)');
  $('g_rho').textContent=S.rho.toFixed(1)+'°'; $('g_lim').textContent=S.lim.toFixed(1)+'°';

  window._S=S; window._T=T; redraw();

  const nAvail=S.st.filter(s=>!s.earth&&!s.sun).length;
  $('state').innerHTML =
    (S.aiming?badge('AIMING','warn'):badge('WAITING (nadir)','ok'))+' &nbsp; '+
    'tilt applied η = <b>'+S.eta.toFixed(1)+'°</b> &nbsp; (ε + margin = '+(S.eps+S.margin).toFixed(1)+'° '+(S.aiming?'&gt;':'&le;')+' 0) &nbsp; '+
    (S.smode==='orbit'?('Sun zenith angle '+S.thetaS.toFixed(0)+'°'+(S.sunEcl?' &middot; '+badge('ECLIPSE','info'):'')):'')+
    '<div style="margin-top:6px">Available trackers now: '+
    (nAvail===0?badge('0 &mdash; FULL STAR-TRACKER BLIND','bad'):badge(nAvail+' / 3',nAvail===3?'ok':'warn'))+'</div>';
  $('stTable').innerHTML='<tr><th>ST</th><th>angle to nadir</th><th>angle to Sun</th><th>status</th></tr>'+
    S.st.map((s,i)=>{
      const col=s.earth?COL.earth:(s.sun?COL.sun:COL.ok);
      const txt=(s.earth?'Earth ':'')+(s.sun?'Sun ':'')||'OK';
      return '<tr><td><span class="sw" style="background:'+col+'"></span>ST'+(i+1)+'</td><td>'+s.angN.toFixed(1)+'° <span style="color:#8b98a8">(need &gt; '+S.lim.toFixed(1)+'°)</span></td><td>'+s.angS.toFixed(1)+'° <span style="color:#8b98a8">(need &gt; 35°)</span></td><td style="color:'+col+'">'+txt.trim()+'</td></tr>';
    }).join('');
  $('tri').innerHTML='<b>Triangle O-S-T</b> (Earth centre, satellite, target): angle at S = η = '+etaT.toFixed(1)+'°, angle at T = 90°+ε = '+(90+S.eps).toFixed(1)+'°, angle at O = λ = '+lam.toFixed(1)+'° &nbsp;(sum = 180°).';

  const etaWc=etaOf(eE+0.001,S.r);
  const W=scan(etaWc,S.r,S.smode,S.beta); S.W=W; S.etaWc=etaWc;
  const full=W.minAvail===0;
  $('worst').innerHTML='<b>Worst case allowed by this margin</b> (tilt η = '+etaWc.toFixed(1)+'°, all φ'+(S.smode==='manual'?', all Sun directions':', all ν &amp; bearings at β = '+S.beta+'°')+'):<br>'+
    'max trackers Earth-blinded: <b>'+W.maxEarth+'</b> &nbsp;|&nbsp; fewest trackers left: <b>'+W.minAvail+'</b> &nbsp; '+
    (full?badge('FULL BLIND POSSIBLE','bad'):badge('SAFE: ≥1 tracker always available','ok'));
  $('thr').innerHTML='<b>Thresholds at '+S.alt+' km</b> (ρ = '+T.rho.toFixed(1)+'°):<br>'+
    '• no Earth blinding: η ≤ '+T.etaNB.toFixed(1)+'° &rArr; ε<sub>min</sub> ≥ <b>'+T.epsNB.toFixed(1)+'°</b> &rArr; margin ≤ <b>'+(-T.epsNB).toFixed(1)+'° ('+(-T.epsNB*D2R).toFixed(3)+' rad)</b><br>'+
    '• ≤1 tracker Earth-blinded: η ≤ '+T.eta2.toFixed(1)+'° &rArr; ε<sub>min</sub> ≥ <b>'+T.eps2.toFixed(1)+'°</b> &rArr; margin ≤ <b>'+(-T.eps2).toFixed(1)+'° ('+(-T.eps2*D2R).toFixed(3)+' rad)</b> (not sufficient on its own, see worst case)<br>'+
    '• margin 0 &rArr; η up to '+T.rho.toFixed(1)+'° (aim down to the horizon)';
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ events
IDS.forEach(i=>$(i).addEventListener('input',update));
document.querySelectorAll('input[name=smode]').forEach(e=>e.addEventListener('change',update));
const setMargin=v=>{ $('margin').value=Math.max(-60,Math.min(30,v)); update(); };
$('btnDefault').onclick=()=>setMargin(0);
$('btn2').onclick=()=>setMargin(-Math.ceil(window._T.eps2*2)/2);
$('btnNB').onclick=()=>setMargin(-Math.ceil(window._T.epsNB*2)/2);
$('btnFind').onclick=()=>{
  const S=window._S, msg=$('findMsg');
  if(S.W.minAvail>0){ msg.innerHTML='No full-blind case exists at this margin/altitude: at least '+S.W.minAvail+' tracker(s) always remain. Try margin = 0.'; return; }
  const a=S.W.arg; $('phi').value=a.phi;
  $('eps').value=Math.min(90,Math.max(0,-S.margin)+0.001);
  if(S.smode==='manual'){ $('ths').value=a.cfg.ths; $('als').value=a.cfg.als; }
  else { $('nu').value=a.cfg.nu; $('brg').value=a.cfg.brg; }
  msg.innerHTML='Set to a configuration where all 3 trackers are blind (Earth and/or Sun). Now raise the margin toward the green curve and watch it disappear.';
  update();
};
$('btnRecenterAll').onclick=()=>{ Object.values(VIEW).forEach(resetView); redraw(); };

// zoom / recenter toolbars, wheel zoom, drag pan and double-click recenter on every plot
document.querySelectorAll('.tb').forEach(tb=>{
  const v=VIEW[tb.dataset.v];
  tb.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{
    const a=b.dataset.a;
    if(a==='reset') resetView(v); else zoomAt(v,a==='in'?1.3:1/1.3,v.cx,v.cy);
    redraw();
  });
});
Object.values(VIEW).forEach(v=>{
  const c=v.el.canvas;
  c.addEventListener('wheel',e=>{ e.preventDefault(); const r=c.getBoundingClientRect();
    zoomAt(v,e.deltaY<0?1.15:1/1.15,e.clientX-r.left,e.clientY-r.top); redraw(); },{passive:false});
  let drag=null;
  c.addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{ drag={x:e.clientX,y:e.clientY}; c.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); });
  c.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{ if(!drag) return; v.tx+=e.clientX-drag.x; v.ty+=e.clientY-drag.y; drag={x:e.clientX,y:e.clientY}; redraw(); });
  c.addEventListener('pointerup',()=>{ drag=null; });
  c.addEventListener('dblclick',()=>{ resetView(v); redraw(); });
});

let sweeping=false, last=0, phiAcc=0;
$('btnSweep').onclick=()=>{ sweeping=!sweeping; $('btnSweep').innerHTML=sweeping?'&#9632; Stop':'&#9654; Sweep φ'; if(sweeping){ last=performance.now(); phiAcc=parseFloat($('phi').value); requestAnimationFrame(tick);} };
function tick(t){ if(!sweeping) return; const dt=(t-last)/1000; last=t;
  phiAcc=(phiAcc+dt*30)%360; $('phi').value=Math.round(phiAcc/5)*5%360; update(); requestAnimationFrame(tick); }

update();
</script>
</body>
</html>